mongodb is a nosql database introduced in 2007
and it stores data in flexible, bson not in tables
it is schema less that is fields can vary across documents
it supports horizontal scaling
it also supports acid property



=how data is stored in mongodb
data is stored in collection
each collection contains documents
documents contains fields stored in bson format



=mongodb is good when
application with rapidly changing schemas
big data and real time analytics 
speed and scalibility is priority
content heavy apps
iot and mobiles apps where data is semi structured
=mongodb is not ideal when
system requires complex transactions across multiple tables
application where data integrity and strict schema are critical
workloads with heavy relational queries
small scale apps where flexibility of mongodb adds unnecessary burden





=how mongodb works
uses a clint server model that is applications connects to mongodb via drivers
supports replica sets for high availability 
uses sharding for horizontal scaling
query language is mongodb query language mql
provides aggregation pipelines for advanced data processing



=mongodb shell
command line interface cli
direct interaction with mongodb using js like commands
runs queries and aggregation pipelines
perform administrative tasks
scriptable 
lightweight and fast but requires knowledges of commands
best for developers, system administrators, and advanced users comfortable with cli




=mongodb compass
graphical user interface gui
visual exploration and management of mongodb databases
full crud functionality 
schema analysis and visualization
real time server stats and performance monitoring
visual explain plans for query optimization
aggregation pipline builder with drag and drop interface
authentication support
best for analysts, beginners or anyone who prefers a visual interface over command line






=mongodb atlas
it is a fully managed cloud database service for mongodb
instead of installing managing and maintaining mongodb on your own local servers or virtual machines, atlas handles all the heavy lifting for you in the cloud like aws, gcp, azure
you can deploy your databases 
it handles routines like patching, backups, configurations
you can scale you databases up or out with few clicks or via an api without any downtime
it includes built in security features like isolation, vpc peering and always on encryption for data at rest and in transit
you can easily deploy clusters in different geographic regions to keep data close to your users for faster performance






=local vs cloud database
mongodb  can be installed locally which will allow you to host own mongodb server on your hardware.
this requires you to manage your server, upgrades and any other maintenance.



























